--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Dependencies (linked or bundled into the shipped artifact)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

490 third-party Rust crates and 31 npm packages, audited 2026-08-08. The resolved set
carries only permissive licenses - MIT, Apache-2.0, BSD, ISC, Zlib, BSL-1.0, Unicode-3.0
- plus MPL-2.0 crates, whose secondary-license clause (MPL 2.0 section 3.3) permits
combination with this program's license. No GPL-2.0-only and no LGPL-only dependency is
in either tree. (`r-efi` offers LGPL-2.1-or-later as one of three options; MIT is taken,
and it is a UEFI-target crate that is not built on macOS at all.)

The authoritative lists are Cargo.lock and bun.lock.

whisper-rs (MIT)
    Rust bindings to whisper.cpp (MIT), which performs speech recognition on-device.
    Linked into the shipped binary. Both carry permissive licenses.
    https://github.com/tazz4843/whisper-rs · https://github.com/ggml-org/whisper.cpp

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Material used at run time, and NOT distributed with this program
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Speech-recognition model weights (ivrit-ai, and any other Whisper-format model)
    Downloaded by the user and loaded at run time. Model weights are not code, are not
    contained in this repository, and are not distributed with this program. They carry
    their own terms, which the user is responsible for accepting.
    https://huggingface.co/ivrit-ai

DictaLM, served through Ollama (Ollama: MIT)
    The Hebrew cleanup pass talks to a local Ollama server over HTTP. Neither Ollama nor
    any model it serves is contained in or distributed with this program.
    https://ollama.com · https://huggingface.co/dicta-il

Anthropic Claude CLI
    Optionally invoked by the offline improvement pass as an evaluation oracle. Not
    contained in or distributed with this program; the user supplies their own
    installation and credentials.
